[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) said one bug: the parser reads dates month first. Its own table already
disagreed, and the report bodies say more. Read them and #4471 held **three problems**, each with
its own fix. Engineering closed #4471 on 5 October: the parser is fixed and the booking-v3 form is
retired. The third problem was never part of either.

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 is closed, but one problem in it is still open: bookings that move by one day. Keep new reports
of it in issue 3, not in #4471.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {issues} />

The counts come from the export at render time, one report per id (the export repeats some).

## The three problems

**`parser`: the shared parser reads every date month first.** Every tenant on file writes the day
first, so any date with a day of 12 or less comes out with day and month swapped: 7 April goes out
as 4 July. It reaches us through every channel and every tenant. **Fixed**
("fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales"); [issue 1](https://github.com/AnnaStanio/mega-s01e03-4471/issues/1)
is closed.

**`hint`: the booking-v3 form tells people to type the month first.** Its date field prints
`MM/DD/YYYY`, people follow it, and the form reads the date day first. Only booking-v3 tenants, only
through the form. The swap happens before the parser, so the parser fix does not touch it. **Won't fix**:
the booking-v3 form is retired, so the hint is gone with it;
[issue 2](https://github.com/AnnaStanio/mega-s01e03-4471/issues/2) is closed as not planned.

**`one-day`: bookings move by one day.** Day and month stay put; the date is a day early or late.
Lisbon sees Tuesday and Toronto sees Monday for the same meeting; an invite arrives before its
booking. That points at time zones, not at the parser. The desk had read these as a one-day move
(`desk-notes.json`) but still counted them under the parser. **Open**: neither the parser fix nor the form's
retirement touches it. Tracked in [issue 3](https://github.com/AnnaStanio/mega-s01e03-4471/issues/3).

## Why it was one ticket

- The [dedupe rule](/kb/triage/dedupe) merges on the subject line. All three problems arrive under
  the same subjects ("Wrong day on the invite", "Dates mixed up"), so the rule cannot tell them
  apart. Only the body and the tenant can.
- Intake's tag is a guess from the reporter's browser, not the tenant. It calls form-hint reports
  `parser` and parser reports `hint`. Place a report by its tenant, its form and its channel.

## What changes on the desk

- #4471 was not one known issue. Closing it closed two problems, not three.
- A new date report: read the body. A date a day off is `one-day`: add it to issue 3. A new day/month
  swap after the parser fix is a regression: open a new ticket, do not reopen #4471.

